signoff_required":false,"topics":["blog","browser","compiler","components","hybrid","nextjs","node","react","server-rendering","ssg","static","static-site-generator","universal","vercel"],"visibility":"public","forks":30029,"open_issues":3156,"watchers":136480,"default_branch":"canary","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/pulls/61392","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/61392","diff_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/61392.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/61392.patch","merged_at":"2024-02-05T00:17:47Z"},"body":"fixes #61390\r\n\r\n### What?\r\n\r\nAdded encodeURIComponent to encode revalidateTag value beforing appending it to the url.\r\n\r\n### Why?\r\n\r\nIf a tag contains special characters the tag wont be revalidated because the special characters arent encoded.\r\nBy encoding the tag any special characters can be used.\r\nCheck out issue #61390 for further explanation\r\n\r\nI believe this is the reason why users report the revalidateTag as unreliable. They might be using special characters in their tags to make sure they are unique, but when deployed to vercel and the fetch cache is used revalidateTag fail to revalidate them.\r\n\r\n### How?\r\n\r\nBy encoding revalidateTag with encodeURIcomponent the tag can contain special characters.\r\n\r\nCloses NEXT-\r\nFixes #61390","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/61392/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/61392/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":11697132750,"node_id":"CE_lADOBC3Cis59pcuUzwAAAAK5NBTO","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/events/11697132750","actor":{"login":"ijjk","id":22380829,"node_